course: dictionary
lesson: 4422
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Hammerhead is one of these words. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «Hammerhead sharks have wide heads with an eye at each end» is about an animal, because sharks and eyes are the clues.
explain: Now read «The hammerhead sweeps the sand for hidden stingrays.» Sweeping the sand and hunting stingrays are clues that it is still the shark. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Hammerhead can also mean the head of a hammer, the heavy metal part you hit with. A third meaning is an African wading bird with a crest at the back of its head. Each meaning has its own clues, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant.
fact: «Hammerhead» means a shark with a wide, flat head shaped like a hammer, with an eye at each end.
fact: «Hammerhead» also means the heavy metal head of a hammer, and it can mean an African wading bird with a crest.
fact: «Schools» means big groups of fish swimming together, as in «a school of hammerheads».
exercise: «Hammerhead sharks have wide heads with an eye at each end.» What is a hammerhead in this sentence? | *A shark with a wide, flat head | A hammer used to hit nails | A small fish that lives in rivers | A bird that wades in water
exercise: «The hammerhead sweeps the sand for hidden stingrays.» What is the hammerhead doing? | Flying over the sea | Hammering a nail into the sand | Building a nest in a tree | *Searching the sand for hidden food
exercise: Find and copy one word that means a big group of fish swimming together. | crest | *schools | wading | electric
test: «Some hammerheads gather in big schools near islands.» What does schools mean here? | Places where children learn | Rows of hammers on a wall | Lessons about the sea | *Big groups of fish swimming together
test: Which meaning fits the head of a tool you hit nails with? | An African bird with a crest | A type of stingray | *The heavy metal part of a hammer | A shark with an eye at each end
exam: Which of these is NOT a meaning of hammerhead? | A shark with a wide, flat head | The heavy metal part of a hammer | *A type of stingray that lives in the sand | An African wading bird with a crest
